  "visual": {
    "visualType": "textbox",
    "objects": {
      "general": [
        {
          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Key findings",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Segoe UI Semibold', wf_segoe-ui_semibold, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "14pt",
                      "color": "#003399"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "1. Combining five models gives the lowest error at 1 day and 1 week; at 1 month HAR-X alone is best.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1A1A1A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "2. Beyond HAR-X the algorithm matters little: at 1 week LightGBM, LSTM and Transformer cannot be told apart from HAR-X statistically (Diebold-Mariano tests) and only the combinations beat it; at 1 day they all beat it, but by 2% at most.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1A1A1A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "3. The Transformer has the lowest average error (MAE) at 1 week and 1 month and is among the best in calm markets, but falls behind in crises: it reacts late when volatility jumps, which QLIKE punishes and MAE does not.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1A1A1A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "4. For risk limits, any volatility model beats historical simulation: with a multiplier learned from the data, the 99% VaR is violated on 1.1-1.2% of days (target 1%).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontFamily": "'Segoe UI', wf_segoe-ui_normal, helvetica, arial, sans-serif",
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1A1A1A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
